response:
\begin{align*}
\cos{B}&=\frac{6}{10}=\frac{3}{5}
\\\Rightarrow\qquad \sin{B}&=\sqrt{1-\cos^2{B}}=\sqrt{1-\frac{9}{25}}=\frac{4}{5}
\\\Rightarrow\qquad \tan{B}&=\frac{\sin{B}}{\cos{B}}=\frac{4}{5}:\frac{3}{5}=\frac{4}{3}
\\\Rightarrow\qquad \tan{C}&=\frac{1}{\tan{B}}=\frac{3}{4}
\end{align*}
Hence, $\boxed{\frac{3}{4}}$.

